window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b278-27a83ed97fb05af6.json"]={sha256:"27a83ed97fb05af61875ba565351e9778217dfff062d4cf3bbfe6d300febcfb1",value:{"id":"b278","title":"魚道水理設計","titleEn":"Hydraulic design of fish passages","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從水池落差、孔口流量與能量密度開始，接續游泳能力、入口誘導、休息區與篩網比較。課程不提供通用魚類流速標準，而要求把魚種、體長、季節和水溫寫入設計條件，並透過偵測率及多段通過率分析，區分水理可行性與真正的遷移成果。","summaryEn":"Start with pool drops, opening discharge and energy density, then examine swimming ability, attraction, resting areas and screening. No universal fish velocity limit is supplied. Species, body size, season and temperature belong in the design conditions. Detection efficiency and passage through multiple reaches distinguish a hydraulically plausible facility from demonstrated migration outcomes.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["池間落差與射流","Pool drops and jet velocity"],["池體積與平均能量密度","Pool volume and mean energy density"],["入口誘導流量比例","Attraction flow proportion"],["篩網接近速度比較","Screen approach velocity comparison"],["多段通行的累積效果","Cumulative passage across reaches"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["池間落差與射流","池體積與平均能量密度","入口誘導流量比例","篩網接近速度比較","多段通行的累積效果"],"labelsEn":["Pool drops and jet velocity","Pool volume and mean energy density","Attraction flow proportion","Screen approach velocity comparison","Cumulative passage across reaches"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課先用「池間落差與射流」建立原創假想基準，再以「開口流量與係數」檢查另一個控制機制。第一組輸入及結果為 g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s；第二組為 Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s。學員需在同一張工作表分列量綱、時間、位置與適用範圍，先核對守恆，再解釋為何兩個得數不能互相代替。最後以第三單元提出的量測設計驗證假設，並將超出模型能力的水理、生態或治理問題列為待研究項目；這些示例並非所列案例的現場實測。敏感度重算：固定 g=9.81 m/s2 與理想無損失假設，將 dh 從 0.15 m 增至 0.18 m，速度由 1.715517 m/s 增至 1.879255 m/s，約增加百分之九點五四。落差增加兩成而速度非增加兩成，且仍未判定魚種可通過性。","textEn":"Begin with an original hypothetical baseline for Pool drops and jet velocity and examine another controlling mechanism through Opening discharge and coefficient. The first inputs and result are g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s; the second are Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s. Keep dimensions, time, location and validity conditions in separate columns of the same working sheet. Check conservation before explaining why the two numerical results cannot substitute for one another. Use the third unit measurement design to test assumptions and identify hydraulic, ecological or governance questions that exceed the model. These examples are not field observations from the named reference cases. Sensitivity recalculation: Keep g=9.81 m/s2 and the ideal loss-free assumption fixed while increasing dh from 0.15 m to 0.18 m. Velocity rises from 1.715517 m/s to 1.879255 m/s, approximately 9.54 percent. A twenty percent drop increase does not produce a twenty percent speed increase and still does not determine species passage suitability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b278-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「池間落差與射流」與「開口流量與係數」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pool drops and jet velocity\" and \"Opening discharge and coefficient\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b278-v15-01","title":"池間落差與射流：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pool drops and jet velocity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「池間落差與射流」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pool drops and jet velocity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"魚道各池之間的水頭差會轉成局部射流動能，分散總落差可以改變每一段的通行負擔。理想能量式只提供速度尺度，真實射流會收縮、耗散並與池內回流互動，不能用它代替魚所選路徑的速度。魚種、體長、水溫與游泳時間共同決定能力，短時爆發速度也不同於可持續速度。設計應先描述目標族群與季節，再把局部水理和可供停留的空間連成一條可走通的路徑。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「池間落差與射流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Head difference between pools creates local jet energy, so dividing total fall changes the challenge at each passage. An ideal energy equation gives a velocity scale, while real jets contract, dissipate and interact with recirculation. It does not describe every route selected by a fish. Species, length, temperature and duration affect swimming ability, and burst speed differs from sustained speed. Define the target population and season before linking hydraulic conditions with connected resting opportunities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pool drops and jet velocity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「池間落差與射流」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pool drops and jet velocity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-01-k1","title":"池間落差與射流","titleEn":"Pool drops and jet velocity","text":"魚道各池之間的水頭差會轉成局部射流動能，分散總落差可以改變每一段的通行負擔。理想能量式只提供速度尺度，真實射流會收縮、耗散並與池內回流互動，不能用它代替魚所選路徑的速度。","textEn":"Head difference between pools creates local jet energy, so dividing total fall changes the challenge at each passage. An ideal energy equation gives a velocity scale, while real jets contract, dissipate and interact with recirculation.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「池間落差與射流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pool drops and jet velocity\" is correct?","options":["池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會","魚道各池之間的水頭差會轉成局部射流動能，分散總落差可以改變每一段的通行負擔。","流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變"],"optionsEn":["Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity","Head difference between pools creates local jet energy, so dividing total fall changes the challenge at each passage.","A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater"],"answer":1,"explanation":"魚道各池之間的水頭差會轉成局部射流動能，分散總落差可以改變每一段的通行負擔。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Head difference between pools creates local jet energy, so dividing total fall changes the challenge at each passage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b278-v15-02","title":"池間落差與射流：定量估算","titleEn":"Pool drops and jet velocity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「池間落差與射流」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pool drops and jet velocity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s。適用邊界：忽略損失的局部速度尺度，不是魚種可通過限值或池內平均流速。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s. Applicable boundary: Local ideal velocity scale without losses, not a species passage limit or pool average. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量相鄰池水位，沿開口與魚可能游經區量測速度分布及水深。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure adjoining levels simultaneously and map velocity and depth across the opening and potential routes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s。適用邊界：忽略損失的局部速度尺度，不是魚種可通過限值或池內平均流速。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s. Applicable boundary: Local ideal velocity scale without losses, not a species passage limit or pool average.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「池間落差與射流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pool drops and jet velocity\", which statement holds?","options":["魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度","名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank","Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b278-v15-03","title":"池間落差與射流：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pool drops and jet velocity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「池間落差與射流」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pool drops and jet velocity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量相鄰池水位，沿開口與魚可能游經區量測速度分布及水深。將瞬時峰值與時間平均分列，並記錄目標魚體長與水溫，避免把一支流速計的平均值當成完整通行環境。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure adjoining levels simultaneously and map velocity and depth across the opening and potential routes. Separate instantaneous peaks from time averages, recording fish length and water temperature so one meter average is not mistaken for the whole passage environment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將落差增加一倍重算理想速度，與速度也加倍的假設比較。畫出一條包含休息區的通行路徑，標示仍需取得的魚種能力及局部流速資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double the drop and compare ideal velocity with a doubled-speed assumption. Draw a connected route including refuges and identify the species-performance and local velocity observations still needed to assess passage.","failure":"注意干擾：射流正面衝向下一開口可能形成連續高速走廊，讓魚無法休息。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A jet aimed directly at the next opening can create a continuous fast corridor without rest. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量相鄰池水位，沿開口與魚可能游經區量測速度分布及水深。將瞬時峰值與時間平均分列，並記錄目標魚體長與水溫，避免把一支流速計的平均值當成完整通行環境。","textEn":"Measure adjoining levels simultaneously and map velocity and depth across the opening and potential routes. Separate instantaneous peaks from time averages, recording fish length and water temperature so one meter average is not mistaken for the whole passage environment.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將落差增加一倍重算理想速度，與速度也加倍的假設比較。畫出一條包含休息區的通行路徑，標示仍需取得的魚種能力及局部流速資料。","textEn":"Double the drop and compare ideal velocity with a doubled-speed assumption. Draw a connected route including refuges and identify the species-performance and local velocity observations still needed to assess passage.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「池間落差與射流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pool drops and jet velocity\"?","options":["同步量相鄰池水位，沿開口與魚可能游經區量測速度分布及水深。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流"],"optionsEn":["Measure adjoining levels simultaneously and map velocity and depth across the opening and potential routes.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步量相鄰池水位，沿開口與魚可能游經區量測速度分布及水深。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure adjoining levels simultaneously and map velocity and depth across the opening and potential routes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b278-v15-04","title":"池間落差與射流：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pool drops and jet velocity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「池間落差與射流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pool drops and jet velocity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"射流正面衝向下一開口可能形成連續高速走廊，讓魚無法休息。即使每池落差相同，也需檢查射流方向及避流區是否彼此連通。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A jet aimed directly at the next opening can create a continuous fast corridor without rest. Equal pool drops therefore still require checking jet orientation and connectivity between lower-velocity refuge areas. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計應先描述目標族群與季節，再把局部水理和可供停留的空間連成一條可走通的路徑。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Define the target population and season before linking hydraulic conditions with connected resting opportunities.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"射流正面衝向下一開口可能形成連續高速走廊，讓魚無法休息。即使每池落差相同，也需檢查射流方向及避流區是否彼此連通。","textEn":"A jet aimed directly at the next opening can create a continuous fast corridor without rest. Equal pool drops therefore still require checking jet orientation and connectivity between lower-velocity refuge areas.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「池間落差與射流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pool drops and jet velocity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","射流正面衝向下一開口可能形成連續高速走廊，讓魚無法休息。","流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A jet aimed directly at the next opening can create a continuous fast corridor without rest.","A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater"],"answer":1,"explanation":"射流正面衝向下一開口可能形成連續高速走廊，讓魚無法休息。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A jet aimed directly at the next opening can create a continuous fast corridor without rest. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b278-v15-05","title":"開口流量與係數：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Opening discharge and coefficient: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「開口流量與係數」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Opening discharge and coefficient” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"魚道開口把水位差轉為流量，流量係數濃縮了收縮與損失，但它會隨開口形狀、邊緣與淹沒狀態改變。用水深乘寬度建立面積之前，要確認開口是否完全被水淹沒，否則出流型態可能不同。相同流量可以經不同面積形成不同速度與剪切分布，因此滿足供水量並不等於滿足通行條件。控制計算應與入口誘導、下游尾水及池內水位一起閉合。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「開口流量與係數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An opening converts level difference into discharge. Its coefficient represents contraction and losses but changes with geometry, edges and submergence. Before using width times height, verify that the opening is fully wetted; otherwise a different flow relation may apply. The same discharge through different areas produces different velocities and shear distributions, so supplying enough water does not establish passage suitability. Close the calculation with attraction flow, tailwater and pool levels instead of treating one opening independently. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Opening discharge and coefficient” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「開口流量與係數」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Opening discharge and coefficient”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-05-k1","title":"開口流量與係數","titleEn":"Opening discharge and coefficient","text":"魚道開口把水位差轉為流量，流量係數濃縮了收縮與損失，但它會隨開口形狀、邊緣與淹沒狀態改變。用水深乘寬度建立面積之前，要確認開口是否完全被水淹沒，否則出流型態可能不同。","textEn":"An opening converts level difference into discharge. Its coefficient represents contraction and losses but changes with geometry, edges and submergence.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「開口流量與係數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Opening discharge and coefficient\" is correct?","options":["流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變","平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同","魚道開口把水位差轉為流量，流量係數濃縮了收縮與損失，但它會隨開口形狀、邊緣與淹沒狀態改變。"],"optionsEn":["A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater","Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool","An opening converts level difference into discharge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"魚道開口把水位差轉為流量，流量係數濃縮了收縮與損失，但它會隨開口形狀、邊緣與淹沒狀態改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An opening converts level difference into discharge. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b278-v15-06","title":"開口流量與係數：定量估算","titleEn":"Opening discharge and coefficient: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「開口流量與係數」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Opening discharge and coefficient” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s。適用邊界：完全淹沒開口與給定有效係數，未把係數當通用常數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Fully submerged opening with an assumed effective coefficient, not a universal coefficient. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在多組水位差下量測流量，反算有效係數並檢查是否隨尾水改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure discharge over several head differences and infer the effective coefficient, checking tailwater dependence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s。適用邊界：完全淹沒開口與給定有效係數，未把係數當通用常數。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Fully submerged opening with an assumed effective coefficient, not a universal coefficient.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「開口流量與係數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Opening discharge and coefficient\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s。","誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比","孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Cd=0.7 dimensionless.","Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance","Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b278-v15-07","title":"開口流量與係數：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Opening discharge and coefficient: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「開口流量與係數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Opening discharge and coefficient” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在多組水位差下量測流量，反算有效係數並檢查是否隨尾水改變。量開口實際尺寸及邊緣損傷，將堵塞與未堵塞資料分開；若係數不穩定，應辨認流態轉換而非只取全部平均。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure discharge over several head differences and infer the effective coefficient, checking tailwater dependence. Survey actual dimensions and edge damage. Separate blocked and clear conditions; unstable coefficients call for identifying regime changes rather than averaging every observation together. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：使有效開口寬度縮小四分之一重算流量，再討論水位差可能隨之改變的情況。列出應同步觀測的池水位，說明為何單一開口不能獨立調整。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce effective width by one quarter and recalculate discharge, then discuss possible changes in head difference. Identify pool levels that require simultaneous observation and explain why one opening cannot always be adjusted independently.","failure":"注意干擾：枝葉堵住部分開口會改變流量與局部高速區，可能使其他池水位也偏離預期。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Debris can reduce opening area while changing local jets and levels in adjoining pools. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在多組水位差下量測流量，反算有效係數並檢查是否隨尾水改變。量開口實際尺寸及邊緣損傷，將堵塞與未堵塞資料分開；若係數不穩定，應辨認流態轉換而非只取全部平均。","textEn":"Measure discharge over several head differences and infer the effective coefficient, checking tailwater dependence. Survey actual dimensions and edge damage. Separate blocked and clear conditions; unstable coefficients call for identifying regime changes rather than averaging every observation together.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"使有效開口寬度縮小四分之一重算流量，再討論水位差可能隨之改變的情況。列出應同步觀測的池水位，說明為何單一開口不能獨立調整。","textEn":"Reduce effective width by one quarter and recalculate discharge, then discuss possible changes in head difference. Identify pool levels that require simultaneous observation and explain why one opening cannot always be adjusted independently.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「開口流量與係數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Opening discharge and coefficient\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在多組水位差下量測流量，反算有效係數並檢查是否隨尾水改變。","上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Measure discharge over several head differences and infer the effective coefficient, checking tailwater dependence.","Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在多組水位差下量測流量，反算有效係數並檢查是否隨尾水改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure discharge over several head differences and infer the effective coefficient, checking tailwater dependence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b278-v15-08","title":"開口流量與係數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Opening discharge and coefficient: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「開口流量與係數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Opening discharge and coefficient” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"枝葉堵住部分開口會改變流量與局部高速區，可能使其他池水位也偏離預期。只按閘門開度推流量會漏掉堵塞造成的網路連鎖反應。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Debris can reduce opening area while changing local jets and levels in adjoining pools. Inferring discharge solely from gate position misses these blockage effects and their propagation through the connected passage system. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：控制計算應與入口誘導、下游尾水及池內水位一起閉合。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Close the calculation with attraction flow, tailwater and pool levels instead of treating one opening independently.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"枝葉堵住部分開口會改變流量與局部高速區，可能使其他池水位也偏離預期。只按閘門開度推流量會漏掉堵塞造成的網路連鎖反應。","textEn":"Debris can reduce opening area while changing local jets and levels in adjoining pools. Inferring discharge solely from gate position misses these blockage effects and their propagation through the connected passage system.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「開口流量與係數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Opening discharge and coefficient\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同","枝葉堵住部分開口會改變流量與局部高速區，可能使其他池水位也偏離預期。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool","Debris can reduce opening area while changing local jets and levels in adjoining pools."],"answer":2,"explanation":"枝葉堵住部分開口會改變流量與局部高速區，可能使其他池水位也偏離預期。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Debris can reduce opening area while changing local jets and levels in adjoining pools. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b278-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「池體積與平均能量密度」與「游泳速度與地面進度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pool volume and mean energy density\" and \"Swimming speed and ground progress\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b278-v15-09","title":"池體積與平均能量密度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pool volume and mean energy density: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「池體積與平均能量密度」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pool volume and mean energy density” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"流量跨越水頭差釋出的功率除以池體積，可形成平均體積能量耗散尺度，方便比較不同配置。這個平均數不表示能量在空間均勻分布，入口射流、渦流中心與底部角落可能差異很大。有效參與混合的水體也可能小於幾何池容，死水區增加體積卻未改善通行。魚類反應還受紊流尺度與方向影響，因此平均功率密度須搭配流場和行為觀察，不應單獨作成效判決。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「池體積與平均能量密度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Discharge falling through a head difference releases power; dividing by pool volume gives a mean volumetric dissipation scale for comparing layouts. Dissipation is not spatially uniform: jets, vortex cores and corners differ. The actively mixed volume may be smaller than geometric volume, so dead zones can enlarge a pool without improving passage. Fish also respond to turbulence scale and direction. Pair the average power density with flow mapping and behaviour instead of making it the sole performance criterion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pool volume and mean energy density” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「池體積與平均能量密度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pool volume and mean energy density”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-09-k1","title":"池體積與平均能量密度","titleEn":"Pool volume and mean energy density","text":"流量跨越水頭差釋出的功率除以池體積，可形成平均體積能量耗散尺度，方便比較不同配置。這個平均數不表示能量在空間均勻分布，入口射流、渦流中心與底部角落可能差異很大。","textEn":"Discharge falling through a head difference releases power; dividing by pool volume gives a mean volumetric dissipation scale for comparing layouts. Dissipation is not spatially uniform: jets, vortex cores and corners differ.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「池體積與平均能量密度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pool volume and mean energy density\" is correct?","options":["流量跨越水頭差釋出的功率除以池體積，可形成平均體積能量耗散尺度，方便比較不同配置。","平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同","魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度"],"optionsEn":["Discharge falling through a head difference releases power; dividing by pool volume gives a mean volumetric dissipation scale for comparing layouts.","Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool","A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank"],"answer":0,"explanation":"流量跨越水頭差釋出的功率除以池體積，可形成平均體積能量耗散尺度，方便比較不同配置。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Discharge falling through a head difference releases power; dividing by pool volume gives a mean volumetric dissipation scale for comparing layouts. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b278-v15-10","title":"池體積與平均能量密度：定量估算","titleEn":"Pool volume and mean energy density: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「池體積與平均能量密度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pool volume and mean energy density” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3。適用邊界：假設該水頭功率全在所列池容內耗散，非魚種允許值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3. Applicable boundary: Assumes the head power dissipates within the stated pool volume; not a species acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量實際池容並排除淤積占據空間，將水位及流量同步記錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure usable volume after sediment accumulation and synchronize levels with discharge.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3。適用邊界：假設該水頭功率全在所列池容內耗散，非魚種允許值。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3. Applicable boundary: Assumes the head power dissipates within the stated pool volume; not a species acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「池體積與平均能量密度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pool volume and mean energy density\", which statement holds?","options":["名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3。","相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流"],"optionsEn":["Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3.","Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b278-v15-11","title":"池體積與平均能量密度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pool volume and mean energy density: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「池體積與平均能量密度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pool volume and mean energy density” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量實際池容並排除淤積占據空間，將水位及流量同步記錄。以流場測量辨認射流核心與死水區，再觀察魚是否使用預期休息區；平均值降低但局部仍猛烈時，需改配置而非只加池深。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure usable volume after sediment accumulation and synchronize levels with discharge. Map jet cores and dead zones, then observe refuge use. If average power decreases while local turbulence remains intense, revise layout rather than simply deepening the pool. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：假設淤積占去半立方公尺重算功率密度，另畫一個總體積更大但死水區更多的池。提出能區分兩種改善是否有效的流場與魚行為量測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Remove half a cubic metre of usable volume and recalculate power density. Sketch a larger pool with more inactive space and propose hydraulic and behavioural measurements that distinguish genuine improvement from a misleading volume increase.","failure":"注意干擾：池底淤積會減少有效體積，使原計算低估平均耗散；另一方面，大死水區也會掩蓋集中紊流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sediment reduces usable volume and can invalidate the original average dissipation estimate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量實際池容並排除淤積占據空間，將水位及流量同步記錄。以流場測量辨認射流核心與死水區，再觀察魚是否使用預期休息區；平均值降低但局部仍猛烈時，需改配置而非只加池深。","textEn":"Measure usable volume after sediment accumulation and synchronize levels with discharge. Map jet cores and dead zones, then observe refuge use. If average power decreases while local turbulence remains intense, revise layout rather than simply deepening the pool.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"假設淤積占去半立方公尺重算功率密度，另畫一個總體積更大但死水區更多的池。提出能區分兩種改善是否有效的流場與魚行為量測。","textEn":"Remove half a cubic metre of usable volume and recalculate power density. Sketch a larger pool with more inactive space and propose hydraulic and behavioural measurements that distinguish genuine improvement from a misleading volume increase.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「池體積與平均能量密度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pool volume and mean energy density\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成","量實際池容並排除淤積占據空間，將水位及流量同步記錄。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent","Measure usable volume after sediment accumulation and synchronize levels with discharge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量實際池容並排除淤積占據空間，將水位及流量同步記錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure usable volume after sediment accumulation and synchronize levels with discharge. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b278-v15-12","title":"池體積與平均能量密度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pool volume and mean energy density: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「池體積與平均能量密度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pool volume and mean energy density” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"池底淤積會減少有效體積，使原計算低估平均耗散；另一方面，大死水區也會掩蓋集中紊流。檢查時需同時看淤積地形與主流混合範圍。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sediment reduces usable volume and can invalidate the original average dissipation estimate. Large inactive zones can also conceal concentrated turbulence, requiring inspection of both deposited material and the region actively mixed by the jet. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：魚類反應還受紊流尺度與方向影響，因此平均功率密度須搭配流場和行為觀察，不應單獨作成效判決。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pair the average power density with flow mapping and behaviour instead of making it the sole performance criterion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"池底淤積會減少有效體積，使原計算低估平均耗散；另一方面，大死水區也會掩蓋集中紊流。檢查時需同時看淤積地形與主流混合範圍。","textEn":"Sediment reduces usable volume and can invalidate the original average dissipation estimate. Large inactive zones can also conceal concentrated turbulence, requiring inspection of both deposited material and the region actively mixed by the jet.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「池體積與平均能量密度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pool volume and mean energy density\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["池底淤積會減少有效體積，使原計算低估平均耗散；另一方面，大死水區也會掩蓋集中紊流。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度"],"optionsEn":["Sediment reduces usable volume and can invalidate the original average dissipation estimate.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank"],"answer":0,"explanation":"池底淤積會減少有效體積，使原計算低估平均耗散；另一方面，大死水區也會掩蓋集中紊流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sediment reduces usable volume and can invalidate the original average dissipation estimate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b278-v15-13","title":"游泳速度與地面進度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Swimming speed and ground progress: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「游泳速度與地面進度」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Swimming speed and ground progress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"魚相對水的游泳速度與水流相對地面的速度是不同參考系，逆流時兩者相減才是向上游的地面進度。若水流接近可維持游速，通過時間會急遽增加；水流更快時，簡化模型便無正向進度。魚可能利用邊界層或間歇爆發，真實軌跡不能由單一平均速度完整描述。計算應把可維持時間與距離一起列出，並明示水溫及體長條件，避免以最高速度替代耐力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「游泳速度與地面進度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Swimming speed relative to water differs from progress relative to the bank. Against a uniform current, subtract flow speed to obtain upstream ground speed. As current approaches sustainable swimming speed, travel time rises sharply; a faster current gives no positive progress in this simplified model. Fish may use boundary layers or bursts, so an average cannot represent every trajectory. State duration, distance, temperature and body size rather than substituting maximum speed for endurance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Swimming speed and ground progress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「游泳速度與地面進度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Swimming speed and ground progress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-13-k1","title":"游泳速度與地面進度","titleEn":"Swimming speed and ground progress","text":"魚相對水的游泳速度與水流相對地面的速度是不同參考系，逆流時兩者相減才是向上游的地面進度。若水流接近可維持游速，通過時間會急遽增加；水流更快時，簡化模型便無正向進度。","textEn":"Swimming speed relative to water differs from progress relative to the bank. Against a uniform current, subtract flow speed to obtain upstream ground speed.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「游泳速度與地面進度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Swimming speed and ground progress\" is correct?","options":["魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度","魚相對水的游泳速度與水流相對地面的速度是不同參考系，逆流時兩者相減才是向上游的地面進度。","誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比"],"optionsEn":["A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank","Swimming speed relative to water differs from progress relative to the bank.","Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"魚相對水的游泳速度與水流相對地面的速度是不同參考系，逆流時兩者相減才是向上游的地面進度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Swimming speed relative to water differs from progress relative to the bank. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b278-v15-14","title":"游泳速度與地面進度：定量估算","titleEn":"Swimming speed and ground progress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「游泳速度與地面進度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Swimming speed and ground progress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s。適用邊界：一維定常逆流與固定可維持游速，未包括轉向與疲勞。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s. Applicable boundary: One-dimensional steady counterflow with fixed sustainable swimming speed, excluding turns and fatigue. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先確認游泳能力資料的魚種、體長、水溫及試驗持續時間，再於候選路徑量流速。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check species, size, temperature and test duration behind the swimming input, then measure current along candidate routes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s。適用邊界：一維定常逆流與固定可維持游速，未包括轉向與疲勞。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s. Applicable boundary: One-dimensional steady counterflow with fixed sustainable swimming speed, excluding turns and fatigue.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「游泳速度與地面進度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Swimming speed and ground progress\", which statement holds?","options":["孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同","上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s。"],"optionsEn":["Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical","Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b278-v15-15","title":"游泳速度與地面進度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Swimming speed and ground progress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「游泳速度與地面進度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Swimming speed and ground progress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先確認游泳能力資料的魚種、體長、水溫及試驗持續時間，再於候選路徑量流速。以追蹤影像取得地面位移與停留時間，若魚利用邊界低速帶，應沿實際路徑比較而非套斷面平均。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check species, size, temperature and test duration behind the swimming input, then measure current along candidate routes. Use tracking to obtain ground displacement and pauses. Fish using low-velocity boundaries should be assessed along their actual trajectories. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將水流提高到每秒一公尺重算時間，再試每秒一點二公尺並解釋分母為零的物理意義。列出可用來驗證固定游速假設的追蹤資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Raise current to one metre per second and recalculate travel time, then examine current equal to swimming speed. Explain the zero denominator physically and identify tracking data that test the fixed-speed assumption.","failure":"注意干擾：以短時爆發游速估整段長距離通過，會低估疲勞與退回的機會。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using burst speed for a long reach underestimates fatigue and retreat. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先確認游泳能力資料的魚種、體長、水溫及試驗持續時間，再於候選路徑量流速。以追蹤影像取得地面位移與停留時間，若魚利用邊界低速帶，應沿實際路徑比較而非套斷面平均。","textEn":"Check species, size, temperature and test duration behind the swimming input, then measure current along candidate routes. Use tracking to obtain ground displacement and pauses. Fish using low-velocity boundaries should be assessed along their actual trajectories.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將水流提高到每秒一公尺重算時間，再試每秒一點二公尺並解釋分母為零的物理意義。列出可用來驗證固定游速假設的追蹤資料。","textEn":"Raise current to one metre per second and recalculate travel time, then examine current equal to swimming speed. Explain the zero denominator physically and identify tracking data that test the fixed-speed assumption.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「游泳速度與地面進度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Swimming speed and ground progress\"?","options":["先確認游泳能力資料的魚種、體長、水溫及試驗持續時間，再於候選路徑量流速。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會"],"optionsEn":["Check species, size, temperature and test duration behind the swimming input, then measure current along candidate routes.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"先確認游泳能力資料的魚種、體長、水溫及試驗持續時間，再於候選路徑量流速。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check species, size, temperature and test duration behind the swimming input, then measure current along candidate routes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b278-v15-16","title":"游泳速度與地面進度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Swimming speed and ground progress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「游泳速度與地面進度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Swimming speed and ground progress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以短時爆發游速估整段長距離通過，會低估疲勞與退回的機會。觀察到魚反覆嘗試後下退時，需檢查持續時間而不只檢查最大流速。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using burst speed for a long reach underestimates fatigue and retreat. Repeated attempts followed by downstream movement call for examining endurance and resting opportunities, not merely the maximum local current. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：計算應把可維持時間與距離一起列出，並明示水溫及體長條件，避免以最高速度替代耐力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: State duration, distance, temperature and body size rather than substituting maximum speed for endurance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以短時爆發游速估整段長距離通過，會低估疲勞與退回的機會。觀察到魚反覆嘗試後下退時，需檢查持續時間而不只檢查最大流速。","textEn":"Using burst speed for a long reach underestimates fatigue and retreat. Repeated attempts followed by downstream movement call for examining endurance and resting opportunities, not merely the maximum local current.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「游泳速度與地面進度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Swimming speed and ground progress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","以短時爆發游速估整段長距離通過，會低估疲勞與退回的機會。","誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using burst speed for a long reach underestimates fatigue and retreat.","Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以短時爆發游速估整段長距離通過，會低估疲勞與退回的機會。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using burst speed for a long reach underestimates fatigue and retreat. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b278-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「入口誘導流量比例」與「水池換水與魚類停留」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Attraction flow proportion\" and \"Water turnover and fish residence\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b278-v15-17","title":"入口誘導流量比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Attraction flow proportion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「入口誘導流量比例」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Attraction flow proportion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"魚道入口需讓目標魚在多股水流中辨認可接近的路徑，誘導流量只是其中一個因素。入口位置、尾水深度、射流方向與附近洩流都會改變魚是否找到入口。流量占河川總流量的比例能描述供水分配，卻不直接量化入口可見度或魚的選擇。相同占比在不同洪水與機組運轉條件下可能產生不同流場，因此應把入口尋找與進入後通過分成兩個評估階段。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「入口誘導流量比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Attraction flow helps fish locate an accessible entrance among competing currents, but location, tailwater depth, jet direction and nearby releases also matter. Its fraction of river discharge describes water allocation, not entrance detectability or fish choice. Identical fractions can create different flow patterns during floods or generating-unit changes. Evaluate finding the entrance separately from passing through the facility, and examine the operating conditions that alter approach routes rather than assuming a fixed ratio guarantees attraction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Attraction flow proportion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「入口誘導流量比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Attraction flow proportion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-17-k1","title":"入口誘導流量比例","titleEn":"Attraction flow proportion","text":"魚道入口需讓目標魚在多股水流中辨認可接近的路徑，誘導流量只是其中一個因素。入口位置、尾水深度、射流方向與附近洩流都會改變魚是否找到入口。","textEn":"Attraction flow helps fish locate an accessible entrance among competing currents, but location, tailwater depth, jet direction and nearby releases also matter. Its fraction of river discharge describes water allocation, not entrance detectability or fish choice.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「入口誘導流量比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Attraction flow proportion\" is correct?","options":["誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比","名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間","魚道入口需讓目標魚在多股水流中辨認可接近的路徑，誘導流量只是其中一個因素。"],"optionsEn":["Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance","Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool","Attraction flow helps fish locate an accessible entrance among competing currents, but location, tailwater depth, jet direction and nearby releases also matter."],"answer":2,"explanation":"魚道入口需讓目標魚在多股水流中辨認可接近的路徑，誘導流量只是其中一個因素。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Attraction flow helps fish locate an accessible entrance among competing currents, but location, tailwater depth, jet direction and nearby releases also matter. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b278-v15-18","title":"入口誘導流量比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Attraction flow proportion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「入口誘導流量比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Attraction flow proportion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless。適用邊界：僅為指定時刻水量比例，不是普遍建議值或吸引成功率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: A discharge fraction at one specified time, not a universal recommendation or attraction success rate. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：於入口外布設流速測線，記錄河川流量及附近出口操作，同時追蹤魚到達、搜尋與進入時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map approach velocities and record river flow and nearby outlet operation while tracking arrival, search and entry times.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless。適用邊界：僅為指定時刻水量比例，不是普遍建議值或吸引成功率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: A discharge fraction at one specified time, not a universal recommendation or attraction success rate.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「入口誘導流量比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Attraction flow proportion\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless。","相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流","每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless.","Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction","If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b278-v15-19","title":"入口誘導流量比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Attraction flow proportion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「入口誘導流量比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Attraction flow proportion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"於入口外布設流速測線，記錄河川流量及附近出口操作，同時追蹤魚到達、搜尋與進入時間。將未找到入口與進入後退出分開統計，並比較不同尾水條件，避免把兩種失敗混成一個通過率。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map approach velocities and record river flow and nearby outlet operation while tracking arrival, search and entry times. Separate failure to find the entrance from retreat after entry, comparing tailwater conditions rather than combining both into one passage statistic. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將河川流量加倍但誘導流量不變，重算比例並說明它不能直接預測成效減半。設計一個同時量水流及搜尋時間的比較試驗，控制魚種與季節。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double river discharge at unchanged attraction flow and recalculate the fraction without assuming success halves. Design a comparison measuring both currents and search time while controlling species and season across observations.","failure":"注意干擾：誘導射流可能被主流偏轉，讓魚聚集在無法進入的位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: The main current can deflect an attraction jet toward an inaccessible location. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"於入口外布設流速測線，記錄河川流量及附近出口操作，同時追蹤魚到達、搜尋與進入時間。將未找到入口與進入後退出分開統計，並比較不同尾水條件，避免把兩種失敗混成一個通過率。","textEn":"Map approach velocities and record river flow and nearby outlet operation while tracking arrival, search and entry times. Separate failure to find the entrance from retreat after entry, comparing tailwater conditions rather than combining both into one passage statistic.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將河川流量加倍但誘導流量不變，重算比例並說明它不能直接預測成效減半。設計一個同時量水流及搜尋時間的比較試驗，控制魚種與季節。","textEn":"Double river discharge at unchanged attraction flow and recalculate the fraction without assuming success halves. Design a comparison measuring both currents and search time while controlling species and season across observations.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「入口誘導流量比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Attraction flow proportion\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","於入口外布設流速測線，記錄河川流量及附近出口操作，同時追蹤魚到達、搜尋與進入時間。","流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Map approach velocities and record river flow and nearby outlet operation while tracking arrival, search and entry times.","A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater"],"answer":1,"explanation":"於入口外布設流速測線，記錄河川流量及附近出口操作，同時追蹤魚到達、搜尋與進入時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map approach velocities and record river flow and nearby outlet operation while tracking arrival, search and entry times. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b278-v15-20","title":"入口誘導流量比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Attraction flow proportion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「入口誘導流量比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Attraction flow proportion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"誘導射流可能被主流偏轉，讓魚聚集在無法進入的位置。此時增加同方向流量未必改善，需查入口位置與可達水深，而不是只提高占比。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"The main current can deflect an attraction jet toward an inaccessible location. Increasing discharge in the same direction may not help; investigate entrance placement and accessible depth instead of only increasing the fraction. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：相同占比在不同洪水與機組運轉條件下可能產生不同流場，因此應把入口尋找與進入後通過分成兩個評估階段。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Evaluate finding the entrance separately from passing through the facility, and examine the operating conditions that alter approach routes rather than assuming a fixed ratio guarantees attraction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"誘導射流可能被主流偏轉，讓魚聚集在無法進入的位置。此時增加同方向流量未必改善，需查入口位置與可達水深，而不是只提高占比。","textEn":"The main current can deflect an attraction jet toward an inaccessible location. Increasing discharge in the same direction may not help; investigate entrance placement and accessible depth instead of only increasing the fraction.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「入口誘導流量比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Attraction flow proportion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間","誘導射流可能被主流偏轉，讓魚聚集在無法進入的位置。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool","The main current can deflect an attraction jet toward an inaccessible location."],"answer":2,"explanation":"誘導射流可能被主流偏轉，讓魚聚集在無法進入的位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"The main current can deflect an attraction jet toward an inaccessible location. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b278-v15-21","title":"水池換水與魚類停留：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Water turnover and fish residence: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「水池換水與魚類停留」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Water turnover and fish residence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"池容除以流量得到名義換水時間，可作水體更新的尺度，但真實水粒子停留時間會因短路與回流形成分布。魚不是被動示蹤物，可能主動停留、避流或反覆進出，所以水的平均換水時間不能代替魚類恢復體力的時間。溶氧與水溫也受外界交換影響，不能只靠較大體積假定適合休息。課程應把幾何池容、有效混合體積與觀測到的行為時間分開記錄。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水池換水與魚類停留」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pool volume divided by discharge gives nominal water turnover time, while short-circuiting and recirculation produce a distribution of particle residence times. Fish are active organisms that can rest, avoid currents or repeatedly enter and leave; hydraulic turnover therefore does not equal recovery time. Oxygen and temperature depend on additional exchanges, so larger volume alone does not establish refuge quality. Keep geometric volume, actively mixed volume and observed behavioural residence as distinct quantities in the assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Water turnover and fish residence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水池換水與魚類停留」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Water turnover and fish residence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-21-k1","title":"水池換水與魚類停留","titleEn":"Water turnover and fish residence","text":"池容除以流量得到名義換水時間，可作水體更新的尺度，但真實水粒子停留時間會因短路與回流形成分布。魚不是被動示蹤物，可能主動停留、避流或反覆進出，所以水的平均換水時間不能代替魚類恢復體力的時間。","textEn":"Pool volume divided by discharge gives nominal water turnover time, while short-circuiting and recirculation produce a distribution of particle residence times. Fish are active organisms that can rest, avoid currents or repeatedly enter and leave; hydraulic turnover therefore does not equal recovery time.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水池換水與魚類停留」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Water turnover and fish residence\" is correct?","options":["池容除以流量得到名義換水時間，可作水體更新的尺度，但真實水粒子停留時間會因短路與回流形成分布。","名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間","孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同"],"optionsEn":["Pool volume divided by discharge gives nominal water turnover time, while short-circuiting and recirculation produce a distribution of particle residence times.","Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool","Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical"],"answer":0,"explanation":"池容除以流量得到名義換水時間，可作水體更新的尺度，但真實水粒子停留時間會因短路與回流形成分布。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pool volume divided by discharge gives nominal water turnover time, while short-circuiting and recirculation produce a distribution of particle residence times. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b278-v15-22","title":"水池換水與魚類停留：定量估算","titleEn":"Water turnover and fish residence: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水池換水與魚類停留」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Water turnover and fish residence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s。適用邊界：名義水體換水尺度，未假設每隻魚或每個水粒子停留二十秒。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s. Applicable boundary: Nominal water turnover scale, without assuming every fish or water particle remains twenty seconds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用適合現場且獲准的示蹤方式量入口與出口濃度曲線，檢查早到峰與長尾。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use an appropriate authorized tracer method to measure inlet and outlet concentration histories, looking for early peaks and long tails.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s。適用邊界：名義水體換水尺度，未假設每隻魚或每個水粒子停留二十秒。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s. Applicable boundary: Nominal water turnover scale, without assuming every fish or water particle remains twenty seconds.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水池換水與魚類停留」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Water turnover and fish residence\", which statement holds?","options":["上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s。","池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會"],"optionsEn":["Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s.","Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b278-v15-23","title":"水池換水與魚類停留：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Water turnover and fish residence: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水池換水與魚類停留」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Water turnover and fish residence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用適合現場且獲准的示蹤方式量入口與出口濃度曲線，檢查早到峰與長尾。同步追蹤魚停留分布並量水溫、溶氧，將水力短路與魚主動休息區分，不能只用一個平均時間判斷池體功能。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use an appropriate authorized tracer method to measure inlet and outlet concentration histories, looking for early peaks and long tails. Track fish residence alongside temperature and oxygen, distinguishing hydraulic short-circuiting from active resting rather than relying on one mean. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持流量不變將池容增加四分之一重算名義時間，畫兩條平均相近但形狀不同的示蹤曲線。說明哪種附加量測可辨認真正可用的休息空間。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase volume by one quarter at fixed flow and recalculate nominal time. Sketch two tracer curves with similar means but different shapes, then identify additional observations that reveal usable resting space for fish.","failure":"注意干擾：主流直接穿池可能使大部分水快速離開，而角落長時間不更新。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Flow can short-circuit across a pool while corner water renews slowly. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用適合現場且獲准的示蹤方式量入口與出口濃度曲線，檢查早到峰與長尾。同步追蹤魚停留分布並量水溫、溶氧，將水力短路與魚主動休息區分，不能只用一個平均時間判斷池體功能。","textEn":"Use an appropriate authorized tracer method to measure inlet and outlet concentration histories, looking for early peaks and long tails. Track fish residence alongside temperature and oxygen, distinguishing hydraulic short-circuiting from active resting rather than relying on one mean.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持流量不變將池容增加四分之一重算名義時間，畫兩條平均相近但形狀不同的示蹤曲線。說明哪種附加量測可辨認真正可用的休息空間。","textEn":"Increase volume by one quarter at fixed flow and recalculate nominal time. Sketch two tracer curves with similar means but different shapes, then identify additional observations that reveal usable resting space for fish.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水池換水與魚類停留」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Water turnover and fish residence\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同","用適合現場且獲准的示蹤方式量入口與出口濃度曲線，檢查早到峰與長尾。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool","Use an appropriate authorized tracer method to measure inlet and outlet concentration histories, looking for early peaks and long tails."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用適合現場且獲准的示蹤方式量入口與出口濃度曲線，檢查早到峰與長尾。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use an appropriate authorized tracer method to measure inlet and outlet concentration histories, looking for early peaks and long tails. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b278-v15-24","title":"水池換水與魚類停留：失效診斷","titleEn":"Water turnover and fish residence: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水池換水與魚類停留」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Water turnover and fish residence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"主流直接穿池可能使大部分水快速離開，而角落長時間不更新。若只看池容除流量，會同時漏掉高速通道與低氧死水區的問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Flow can short-circuit across a pool while corner water renews slowly. Volume divided by discharge alone then conceals both a fast corridor and stagnant areas that may develop unsuitable oxygen conditions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：課程應把幾何池容、有效混合體積與觀測到的行為時間分開記錄。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Keep geometric volume, actively mixed volume and observed behavioural residence as distinct quantities in the assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"主流直接穿池可能使大部分水快速離開，而角落長時間不更新。若只看池容除流量，會同時漏掉高速通道與低氧死水區的問題。","textEn":"Flow can short-circuit across a pool while corner water renews slowly. Volume divided by discharge alone then conceals both a fast corridor and stagnant areas that may develop unsuitable oxygen conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水池換水與魚類停留」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Water turnover and fish residence\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["主流直接穿池可能使大部分水快速離開，而角落長時間不更新。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同"],"optionsEn":["Flow can short-circuit across a pool while corner water renews slowly.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical"],"answer":0,"explanation":"主流直接穿池可能使大部分水快速離開，而角落長時間不更新。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Flow can short-circuit across a pool while corner water renews slowly. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b278-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「篩網接近速度比較」與「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Screen approach velocity comparison\" and \"Eddy scales and fish size\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b278-v15-25","title":"篩網接近速度比較：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Screen approach velocity comparison: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「篩網接近速度比較」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Screen approach velocity comparison” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"取水篩網與上溯魚道目的不同，前者常需避免魚被吸附或帶入取水口，不能把魚道開口流速直接當成篩網標準。接近速度應相對篩網法向定義，而掃流沿網面方向，兩者對魚的作用不同。以總流量除有效開孔面積得到孔隙平均速度，與按整體網面積計算的表觀速度也不同。教材必須明確標示所用面積和速度定義，才能與指定魚種及生命期的評估方法比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「篩網接近速度比較」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Intake screens and upstream fish passages serve different purposes; a passage-opening velocity cannot simply become a screen criterion. Approach velocity is normal to the screen, while sweeping velocity runs along it. Dividing discharge by effective open area gives a mean opening velocity, distinct from superficial velocity based on gross screen area. State both area and velocity definitions explicitly before comparing with an evaluation method for a particular species and life stage or interpreting blockage effects. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Screen approach velocity comparison” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「篩網接近速度比較」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Screen approach velocity comparison”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-25-k1","title":"篩網接近速度比較","titleEn":"Screen approach velocity comparison","text":"取水篩網與上溯魚道目的不同，前者常需避免魚被吸附或帶入取水口，不能把魚道開口流速直接當成篩網標準。接近速度應相對篩網法向定義，而掃流沿網面方向，兩者對魚的作用不同。","textEn":"Intake screens and upstream fish passages serve different purposes; a passage-opening velocity cannot simply become a screen criterion. Approach velocity is normal to the screen, while sweeping velocity runs along it.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「篩網接近速度比較」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Screen approach velocity comparison\" is correct?","options":["孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同","取水篩網與上溯魚道目的不同，前者常需避免魚被吸附或帶入取水口，不能把魚道開口流速直接當成篩網標準。","相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流"],"optionsEn":["Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical","Intake screens and upstream fish passages serve different purposes; a passage-opening velocity cannot simply become a screen criterion.","Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"取水篩網與上溯魚道目的不同，前者常需避免魚被吸附或帶入取水口，不能把魚道開口流速直接當成篩網標準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Intake screens and upstream fish passages serve different purposes; a passage-opening velocity cannot simply become a screen criterion. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b278-v15-26","title":"篩網接近速度比較：定量估算","titleEn":"Screen approach velocity comparison: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「篩網接近速度比較」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Screen approach velocity comparison” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s。適用邊界：均勻法向通流的孔隙平均速度，不與總網面表觀接近速度混稱。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s. Applicable boundary: Mean opening velocity for uniform normal flow, distinct from gross-area superficial approach velocity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先記錄網面總面積、開孔比例及堵塞分布，再依評估方法在網前規定位置量法向與切向速度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record gross area, open fraction and blockage pattern, then measure normal and tangential velocities at locations specified by the evaluation method.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s。適用邊界：均勻法向通流的孔隙平均速度，不與總網面表觀接近速度混稱。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s. Applicable boundary: Mean opening velocity for uniform normal flow, distinct from gross-area superficial approach velocity.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「篩網接近速度比較」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Screen approach velocity comparison\", which statement holds?","options":["每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成","流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent","A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b278-v15-27","title":"篩網接近速度比較：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Screen approach velocity comparison: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「篩網接近速度比較」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Screen approach velocity comparison” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先記錄網面總面積、開孔比例及堵塞分布，再依評估方法在網前規定位置量法向與切向速度。比較孔隙平均與表觀速度時標出定義，避免把兩種不同面積基準的數字當成儀器不一致。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record gross area, open fraction and blockage pattern, then measure normal and tangential velocities at locations specified by the evaluation method. Label opening and superficial velocities explicitly so different area bases are not mistaken for inconsistent instruments. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將開孔比例降低到零點四重算孔隙速度，另算總網面表觀速度並比較。畫出局部堵塞可能形成的高流速區，說明應如何加密量測而非只取平均。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce open fraction to zero point four and recalculate opening velocity, then compare with gross-area superficial velocity. Sketch a blockage-induced fast region and propose denser measurements instead of relying only on the average.","failure":"注意干擾：局部堵塞會把流量集中到剩餘開孔，平均全網速度可能仍低卻出現高吸附區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Local blockage concentrates flow through remaining openings even when the gross-area average appears modest. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先記錄網面總面積、開孔比例及堵塞分布，再依評估方法在網前規定位置量法向與切向速度。比較孔隙平均與表觀速度時標出定義，避免把兩種不同面積基準的數字當成儀器不一致。","textEn":"Record gross area, open fraction and blockage pattern, then measure normal and tangential velocities at locations specified by the evaluation method. Label opening and superficial velocities explicitly so different area bases are not mistaken for inconsistent instruments.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將開孔比例降低到零點四重算孔隙速度，另算總網面表觀速度並比較。畫出局部堵塞可能形成的高流速區，說明應如何加密量測而非只取平均。","textEn":"Reduce open fraction to zero point four and recalculate opening velocity, then compare with gross-area superficial velocity. Sketch a blockage-induced fast region and propose denser measurements instead of relying only on the average.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「篩網接近速度比較」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Screen approach velocity comparison\"?","options":["先記錄網面總面積、開孔比例及堵塞分布，再依評估方法在網前規定位置量法向與切向速度。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度"],"optionsEn":["Record gross area, open fraction and blockage pattern, then measure normal and tangential velocities at locations specified by the evaluation method.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank"],"answer":0,"explanation":"先記錄網面總面積、開孔比例及堵塞分布，再依評估方法在網前規定位置量法向與切向速度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record gross area, open fraction and blockage pattern, then measure normal and tangential velocities at locations specified by the evaluation method. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b278-v15-28","title":"篩網接近速度比較：失效診斷","titleEn":"Screen approach velocity comparison: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「篩網接近速度比較」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Screen approach velocity comparison” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部堵塞會把流量集中到剩餘開孔，平均全網速度可能仍低卻出現高吸附區。診斷應看空間分布及清污狀態，不能只查總取水量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Local blockage concentrates flow through remaining openings even when the gross-area average appears modest. Investigate spatial velocity patterns and cleaning condition rather than relying solely on total intake discharge or nominal screen area. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：教材必須明確標示所用面積和速度定義，才能與指定魚種及生命期的評估方法比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: State both area and velocity definitions explicitly before comparing with an evaluation method for a particular species and life stage or interpreting blockage effects.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部堵塞會把流量集中到剩餘開孔，平均全網速度可能仍低卻出現高吸附區。診斷應看空間分布及清污狀態，不能只查總取水量。","textEn":"Local blockage concentrates flow through remaining openings even when the gross-area average appears modest. Investigate spatial velocity patterns and cleaning condition rather than relying solely on total intake discharge or nominal screen area.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「篩網接近速度比較」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Screen approach velocity comparison\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","局部堵塞會把流量集中到剩餘開孔，平均全網速度可能仍低卻出現高吸附區。","相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Local blockage concentrates flow through remaining openings even when the gross-area average appears modest.","Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部堵塞會把流量集中到剩餘開孔，平均全網速度可能仍低卻出現高吸附區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Local blockage concentrates flow through remaining openings even when the gross-area average appears modest. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b278-v15-29","title":"渦流尺度與魚體尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Eddy scales and fish size: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Eddy scales and fish size” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"紊流不只由速度大小決定，渦流的空間尺度、持續時間及方向都可能影響魚維持姿態的能力。以特徵長度除以速度擾動可建立周轉時間尺度，但這不是魚的疲勞時間，也不是特定物種的允許週期。渦流尺寸相對魚體長度可能改變作用方式，因此測量應保留空間與時間解析度。過度平均會消除瞬時結構，反之短紀錄又可能把偶發渦流當成代表狀態，需要兼顧兩者。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Turbulence affects posture through spatial scale, duration and direction as well as velocity magnitude. Dividing a characteristic length by velocity fluctuation gives an eddy turnover scale, not fish fatigue time or a species acceptance period. Eddy size relative to body length can change the interaction, so measurements need suitable spatial and temporal resolution. Excessive averaging removes transient structures, whereas very short records may mistake a rare event for typical conditions; both sampling limits require attention. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Eddy scales and fish size” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Eddy scales and fish size”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-29-k1","title":"渦流尺度與魚體尺度","titleEn":"Eddy scales and fish size","text":"紊流不只由速度大小決定，渦流的空間尺度、持續時間及方向都可能影響魚維持姿態的能力。以特徵長度除以速度擾動可建立周轉時間尺度，但這不是魚的疲勞時間，也不是特定物種的允許週期。","textEn":"Turbulence affects posture through spatial scale, duration and direction as well as velocity magnitude. Dividing a characteristic length by velocity fluctuation gives an eddy turnover scale, not fish fatigue time or a species acceptance period.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Eddy scales and fish size\" is correct?","options":["相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流","上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率","紊流不只由速度大小決定，渦流的空間尺度、持續時間及方向都可能影響魚維持姿態的能力。"],"optionsEn":["Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction","Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability","Turbulence affects posture through spatial scale, duration and direction as well as velocity magnitude."],"answer":2,"explanation":"紊流不只由速度大小決定，渦流的空間尺度、持續時間及方向都可能影響魚維持姿態的能力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Turbulence affects posture through spatial scale, duration and direction as well as velocity magnitude. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b278-v15-30","title":"渦流尺度與魚體尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Eddy scales and fish size: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Eddy scales and fish size” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s。適用邊界：量綱尺度估算，非完整紊流頻譜或魚類生理反應模型。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s. Applicable boundary: Dimensional scale estimate, not a complete turbulence spectrum or physiological response model. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在魚可能利用的路徑採集足夠長的高速流速序列，說明取樣頻率與探頭空間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Collect sufficiently long high-rate velocity records along likely routes, documenting sampling frequency and probe spacing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s。適用邊界：量綱尺度估算，非完整紊流頻譜或魚類生理反應模型。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s. Applicable boundary: Dimensional scale estimate, not a complete turbulence spectrum or physiological response model.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Eddy scales and fish size\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s。","池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會","平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s.","Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity","Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b278-v15-31","title":"渦流尺度與魚體尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Eddy scales and fish size: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Eddy scales and fish size” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在魚可能利用的路徑採集足夠長的高速流速序列，說明取樣頻率與探頭空間。比較不同位置的變動與相干性，再將影像中的魚體轉向和時間序列對齊，避免只憑均速推論紊流影響。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Collect sufficiently long high-rate velocity records along likely routes, documenting sampling frequency and probe spacing. Compare fluctuations and coherence across locations, then align fish turning observations with the records rather than inferring turbulence effects from mean velocity alone. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將擾動速度增加一倍重算周轉尺度，並比較兩種魚體長度與渦流尺寸的相對大小。提出能檢驗姿態變化與水流擾動時間關係的同步觀測方案。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double fluctuation velocity and recompute turnover scale. Compare eddy size with two fish lengths and propose synchronized observations that test the timing between hydraulic fluctuations and changes in fish posture along the route.","failure":"注意干擾：探頭取樣過慢會漏掉快速擾動，過大的空間平均又會抹平渦流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Slow sampling can miss rapid fluctuations, and broad spatial averaging can erase eddies. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在魚可能利用的路徑採集足夠長的高速流速序列，說明取樣頻率與探頭空間。比較不同位置的變動與相干性，再將影像中的魚體轉向和時間序列對齊，避免只憑均速推論紊流影響。","textEn":"Collect sufficiently long high-rate velocity records along likely routes, documenting sampling frequency and probe spacing. Compare fluctuations and coherence across locations, then align fish turning observations with the records rather than inferring turbulence effects from mean velocity alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將擾動速度增加一倍重算周轉尺度，並比較兩種魚體長度與渦流尺寸的相對大小。提出能檢驗姿態變化與水流擾動時間關係的同步觀測方案。","textEn":"Double fluctuation velocity and recompute turnover scale. Compare eddy size with two fish lengths and propose synchronized observations that test the timing between hydraulic fluctuations and changes in fish posture along the route.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Eddy scales and fish size\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在魚可能利用的路徑採集足夠長的高速流速序列，說明取樣頻率與探頭空間。","誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Collect sufficiently long high-rate velocity records along likely routes, documenting sampling frequency and probe spacing.","Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在魚可能利用的路徑採集足夠長的高速流速序列，說明取樣頻率與探頭空間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Collect sufficiently long high-rate velocity records along likely routes, documenting sampling frequency and probe spacing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b278-v15-32","title":"渦流尺度與魚體尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Eddy scales and fish size: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Eddy scales and fish size” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"探頭取樣過慢會漏掉快速擾動，過大的空間平均又會抹平渦流。若魚明顯失衡而紀錄平穩，應先查解析度及位置，而非否定行為觀察。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Slow sampling can miss rapid fluctuations, and broad spatial averaging can erase eddies. If fish lose posture while records appear smooth, examine resolution and location before dismissing the behavioural evidence as unreliable. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：過度平均會消除瞬時結構，反之短紀錄又可能把偶發渦流當成代表狀態，需要兼顧兩者。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Excessive averaging removes transient structures, whereas very short records may mistake a rare event for typical conditions; both sampling limits require attention.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"探頭取樣過慢會漏掉快速擾動，過大的空間平均又會抹平渦流。若魚明顯失衡而紀錄平穩，應先查解析度及位置，而非否定行為觀察。","textEn":"Slow sampling can miss rapid fluctuations, and broad spatial averaging can erase eddies. If fish lose posture while records appear smooth, examine resolution and location before dismissing the behavioural evidence as unreliable.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Eddy scales and fish size\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率","探頭取樣過慢會漏掉快速擾動，過大的空間平均又會抹平渦流。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability","Slow sampling can miss rapid fluctuations, and broad spatial averaging can erase eddies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"探頭取樣過慢會漏掉快速擾動，過大的空間平均又會抹平渦流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Slow sampling can miss rapid fluctuations, and broad spatial averaging can erase eddies. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b278-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「偵測效率與通過比例」與「多段通行的累積效果」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Detection efficiency and passage proportion\" and \"Cumulative passage across reaches\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b278-v15-33","title":"偵測效率與通過比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Detection efficiency and passage proportion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「偵測效率與通過比例」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Detection efficiency and passage proportion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"上下游感測站看到的魚數同時受到真實通過及偵測效率影響，直接相除可能把儀器差異誤認為生物損失。用已估偵測機率修正計數，是在同一受追蹤族群、單次計數及相容觀測期間下的簡化估計。重複通過、標記脫落與不同魚種的可偵測性會破壞這些假設。分析需保存個體識別及時間順序，並把尋找入口、進入和完成通過分別定義，才能解釋比例代表什麼。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「偵測效率與通過比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Counts at upstream and downstream detectors combine actual passage with detection efficiency, so a raw ratio can mistake instrumentation differences for biological loss. Correcting counts by estimated detection probabilities is a simplified estimator for one tracked cohort, unique counts and compatible observation windows. Repeated passages, tag loss and species-dependent detectability violate those assumptions. Preserve individual identities and event order, and distinguish attraction, entry and completed passage so the estimated proportion has a clear denominator and interpretation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Detection efficiency and passage proportion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「偵測效率與通過比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Detection efficiency and passage proportion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-33-k1","title":"偵測效率與通過比例","titleEn":"Detection efficiency and passage proportion","text":"上下游感測站看到的魚數同時受到真實通過及偵測效率影響，直接相除可能把儀器差異誤認為生物損失。用已估偵測機率修正計數，是在同一受追蹤族群、單次計數及相容觀測期間下的簡化估計。","textEn":"Counts at upstream and downstream detectors combine actual passage with detection efficiency, so a raw ratio can mistake instrumentation differences for biological loss. Correcting counts by estimated detection probabilities is a simplified estimator for one tracked cohort, unique counts and compatible observation windows.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「偵測效率與通過比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Detection efficiency and passage proportion\" is correct?","options":["上下游感測站看到的魚數同時受到真實通過及偵測效率影響，直接相除可能把儀器差異誤認為生物損失。","上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率","每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成"],"optionsEn":["Counts at upstream and downstream detectors combine actual passage with detection efficiency, so a raw ratio can mistake instrumentation differences for biological loss.","Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability","If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent"],"answer":0,"explanation":"上下游感測站看到的魚數同時受到真實通過及偵測效率影響，直接相除可能把儀器差異誤認為生物損失。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Counts at upstream and downstream detectors combine actual passage with detection efficiency, so a raw ratio can mistake instrumentation differences for biological loss. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b278-v15-34","title":"偵測效率與通過比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Detection efficiency and passage proportion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「偵測效率與通過比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Detection efficiency and passage proportion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless。適用邊界：同一族群唯一個體計數與已知偵測機率的簡化估計，不含估計不確定性。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Simplified same-cohort unique-count estimator with known detection probabilities, excluding estimation uncertainty. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以重複天線或獨立影像估偵測效率，檢查漏測是否隨流量、魚體大小或標記方向改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Estimate detection with redundant antennas or independent imagery and test dependence on discharge, size and tag orientation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless。適用邊界：同一族群唯一個體計數與已知偵測機率的簡化估計，不含估計不確定性。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Simplified same-cohort unique-count estimator with known detection probabilities, excluding estimation uncertainty.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「偵測效率與通過比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Detection efficiency and passage proportion\", which statement holds?","options":["流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless。","魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度"],"optionsEn":["A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nu=80 fish.","A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b278-v15-35","title":"偵測效率與通過比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Detection efficiency and passage proportion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「偵測效率與通過比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Detection efficiency and passage proportion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以重複天線或獨立影像估偵測效率，檢查漏測是否隨流量、魚體大小或標記方向改變。清理重複個體並對齊觀測窗，另報修正比例的不確定性，若結果超過一應查假設而非強制截斷掩蓋問題。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Estimate detection with redundant antennas or independent imagery and test dependence on discharge, size and tag orientation. Deduplicate individuals and align observation windows. Report uncertainty; estimates above one require investigating assumptions rather than silently truncating the result. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將上游偵測率改成零點九重算並與原始比例比較。列出需要保留的個體欄位，再設計一項檢查以辨認漏測、重複計數與真正未通過三種情況。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change upstream detection probability to zero point nine and compare the corrected and raw ratios. List required individual records and design a check separating missed detections, repeated counts and genuine failure to complete passage.","failure":"注意干擾：下游偵測效率較低時，分母被低估會誇大通過率。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Poor downstream detection reduces the denominator and inflates apparent passage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以重複天線或獨立影像估偵測效率，檢查漏測是否隨流量、魚體大小或標記方向改變。清理重複個體並對齊觀測窗，另報修正比例的不確定性，若結果超過一應查假設而非強制截斷掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Estimate detection with redundant antennas or independent imagery and test dependence on discharge, size and tag orientation. Deduplicate individuals and align observation windows. Report uncertainty; estimates above one require investigating assumptions rather than silently truncating the result.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將上游偵測率改成零點九重算並與原始比例比較。列出需要保留的個體欄位，再設計一項檢查以辨認漏測、重複計數與真正未通過三種情況。","textEn":"Change upstream detection probability to zero point nine and compare the corrected and raw ratios. List required individual records and design a check separating missed detections, repeated counts and genuine failure to complete passage.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「偵測效率與通過比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Detection efficiency and passage proportion\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間","以重複天線或獨立影像估偵測效率，檢查漏測是否隨流量、魚體大小或標記方向改變。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool","Estimate detection with redundant antennas or independent imagery and test dependence on discharge, size and tag orientation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以重複天線或獨立影像估偵測效率，檢查漏測是否隨流量、魚體大小或標記方向改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Estimate detection with redundant antennas or independent imagery and test dependence on discharge, size and tag orientation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b278-v15-36","title":"偵測效率與通過比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Detection efficiency and passage proportion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「偵測效率與通過比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Detection efficiency and passage proportion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"下游偵測效率較低時，分母被低估會誇大通過率。若把反覆往返同一魚當不同個體，還可能得到表面大於全部進入數的錯誤成果。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Poor downstream detection reduces the denominator and inflates apparent passage. Counting repeated movements of one fish as separate individuals can further produce an implausible number of successes relative to the original cohort. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：分析需保存個體識別及時間順序，並把尋找入口、進入和完成通過分別定義，才能解釋比例代表什麼。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Preserve individual identities and event order, and distinguish attraction, entry and completed passage so the estimated proportion has a clear denominator and interpretation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"下游偵測效率較低時，分母被低估會誇大通過率。若把反覆往返同一魚當不同個體，還可能得到表面大於全部進入數的錯誤成果。","textEn":"Poor downstream detection reduces the denominator and inflates apparent passage. Counting repeated movements of one fish as separate individuals can further produce an implausible number of successes relative to the original cohort.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「偵測效率與通過比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Detection efficiency and passage proportion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["下游偵測效率較低時，分母被低估會誇大通過率。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成"],"optionsEn":["Poor downstream detection reduces the denominator and inflates apparent passage.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent"],"answer":0,"explanation":"下游偵測效率較低時，分母被低估會誇大通過率。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Poor downstream detection reduces the denominator and inflates apparent passage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b278-v15-37","title":"多段通行的累積效果：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cumulative passage across reaches: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「多段通行的累積效果」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cumulative passage across reaches” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"流域中的多個障礙會把單處看似很高的通過率累積成較低的整體成功率，但乘法必須使用相容的條件機率。若每段數值是已到達該段魚群的通過機率，連乘可表示依序完成的比例；若只是不同調查族群的平均值，就未必可直接相乘。等待與繞行也會延長遷移時間，即使最後通過仍可能錯過繁殖窗口。改善排序應同時考慮瓶頸、時序與族群差異，而非只追求單處漂亮數字。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「多段通行的累積效果」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Multiple barriers can turn high local passage into modest basin-wide success, but multiplication requires compatible conditional probabilities. If each value describes fish that actually reach that stage, their product represents sequential completion; averages from unrelated populations need not be compatible. Delays and detours also matter because eventual passage can miss a breeding window. Prioritize improvements using bottlenecks, timing and population differences rather than optimizing one attractive local percentage without considering the connected migration route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cumulative passage across reaches” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「多段通行的累積效果」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cumulative passage across reaches”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-37-k1","title":"多段通行的累積效果","titleEn":"Cumulative passage across reaches","text":"流域中的多個障礙會把單處看似很高的通過率累積成較低的整體成功率，但乘法必須使用相容的條件機率。若每段數值是已到達該段魚群的通過機率，連乘可表示依序完成的比例；若只是不同調查族群的平均值，就未必可直接相乘。","textEn":"Multiple barriers can turn high local passage into modest basin-wide success, but multiplication requires compatible conditional probabilities. If each value describes fish that actually reach that stage, their product represents sequential completion; averages from unrelated populations need not be compatible.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「多段通行的累積效果」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cumulative passage across reaches\" is correct?","options":["每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成","流域中的多個障礙會把單處看似很高的通過率累積成較低的整體成功率，但乘法必須使用相容的條件機率。","池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會"],"optionsEn":["If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent","Multiple barriers can turn high local passage into modest basin-wide success, but multiplication requires compatible conditional probabilities.","Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity"],"answer":1,"explanation":"流域中的多個障礙會把單處看似很高的通過率累積成較低的整體成功率，但乘法必須使用相容的條件機率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Multiple barriers can turn high local passage into modest basin-wide success, but multiplication requires compatible conditional probabilities. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b278-v15-38","title":"多段通行的累積效果：定量估算","titleEn":"Cumulative passage across reaches: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「多段通行的累積效果」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cumulative passage across reaches” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless。適用邊界：五段條件通過率皆給定相同值；若視為邊際率則另需獨立性假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: All five conditional stage probabilities are assumed equal; using marginal rates instead would additionally require independence. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對同一標記族群建立各段到達及通過的時間表，分母使用真正到達該段的個體。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build arrival and completion histories for the same tagged cohort, using actual arrivals as each denominator.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless。適用邊界：五段條件通過率皆給定相同值；若視為邊際率則另需獨立性假設。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: All five conditional stage probabilities are assumed equal; using marginal rates instead would additionally require independence.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「多段通行的累積效果」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cumulative passage across reaches\", which statement holds?","options":["平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同","誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless。"],"optionsEn":["Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool","Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b278-v15-39","title":"多段通行的累積效果：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cumulative passage across reaches: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「多段通行的累積效果」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cumulative passage across reaches” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對同一標記族群建立各段到達及通過的時間表，分母使用真正到達該段的個體。檢查魚體狀態與季節是否逐段改變，將累積成功與總延遲分開報告，並追查失聯是否只是偵測不足。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build arrival and completion histories for the same tagged cohort, using actual arrivals as each denominator. Check changing condition and season across stages. Report cumulative completion separately from total delay and investigate whether disappearance reflects inadequate detection rather than loss. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將其中一段條件通過率提高到零點九八重算全程比例，再比較減少等待時間但不改通過率的方案。說明兩種效益需要哪些不同觀測才能評估。","observationEn":"Site practice: Raise one conditional stage probability to zero point nine eight and recompute completion. Compare this with reducing delay at unchanged passage probability, identifying the different observations required to evaluate these two benefits.","failure":"注意干擾：某段延遲可能改變下一段面對的流量或季節，讓從其他年份搬來的局部通過率不適用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Delay at one barrier can change the flow or season encountered next, invalidating local rates borrowed from another year. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對同一標記族群建立各段到達及通過的時間表，分母使用真正到達該段的個體。檢查魚體狀態與季節是否逐段改變，將累積成功與總延遲分開報告，並追查失聯是否只是偵測不足。","textEn":"Build arrival and completion histories for the same tagged cohort, using actual arrivals as each denominator. Check changing condition and season across stages. Report cumulative completion separately from total delay and investigate whether disappearance reflects inadequate detection rather than loss.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將其中一段條件通過率提高到零點九八重算全程比例，再比較減少等待時間但不改通過率的方案。說明兩種效益需要哪些不同觀測才能評估。","textEn":"Raise one conditional stage probability to zero point nine eight and recompute completion. Compare this with reducing delay at unchanged passage probability, identifying the different observations required to evaluate these two benefits.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「多段通行的累積效果」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cumulative passage across reaches\"?","options":["對同一標記族群建立各段到達及通過的時間表，分母使用真正到達該段的個體。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同"],"optionsEn":["Build arrival and completion histories for the same tagged cohort, using actual arrivals as each denominator.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical"],"answer":0,"explanation":"對同一標記族群建立各段到達及通過的時間表，分母使用真正到達該段的個體。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build arrival and completion histories for the same tagged cohort, using actual arrivals as each denominator. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b278-v15-40","title":"多段通行的累積效果：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cumulative passage across reaches: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「多段通行的累積效果」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cumulative passage across reaches” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"某段延遲可能改變下一段面對的流量或季節，讓從其他年份搬來的局部通過率不適用。只連乘公布百分比會忽略這種跨段與跨時影響。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Delay at one barrier can change the flow or season encountered next, invalidating local rates borrowed from another year. Multiplying published percentages without cohort and timing checks can therefore misrepresent cumulative migration outcomes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：改善排序應同時考慮瓶頸、時序與族群差異，而非只追求單處漂亮數字。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Prioritize improvements using bottlenecks, timing and population differences rather than optimizing one attractive local percentage without considering the connected migration route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"某段延遲可能改變下一段面對的流量或季節，讓從其他年份搬來的局部通過率不適用。只連乘公布百分比會忽略這種跨段與跨時影響。","textEn":"Delay at one barrier can change the flow or season encountered next, invalidating local rates borrowed from another year. Multiplying published percentages without cohort and timing checks can therefore misrepresent cumulative migration outcomes.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「多段通行的累積效果」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cumulative passage across reaches\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","某段延遲可能改變下一段面對的流量或季節，讓從其他年份搬來的局部通過率不適用。","池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Delay at one barrier can change the flow or season encountered next, invalidating local rates borrowed from another year.","Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity"],"answer":1,"explanation":"某段延遲可能改變下一段面對的流量或季節，讓從其他年份搬來的局部通過率不適用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Delay at one barrier can change the flow or season encountered next, invalidating local rates borrowed from another year. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
